  <!-- EN: Catholicism is the largest branch of Christianity, tracing its origins to the teachings of Jesus Christ and the apostolic succession of Saint Peter, regarded as the first Pope. Centered in Rome and governed by the Papacy, Catholicism developed as the dominant form of Western Christianity throughout the Middle Ages, shaping the spiritual, cultural, and political foundations of Europe. The Catholic Church emphasizes the authority of Scripture and Tradition, upheld by the Magisterium (teaching authority of the Church). Faith and reason are viewed as complementary paths to divine truth, a view deeply rooted in the scholastic philosophy of medieval theologians such as Thomas Aquinas and Augustine of Hippo. Medieval Catholicism was defined by its elaborate rituals, veneration of saints, and a strong emphasis on salvation through faith, good works, and participation in the sacraments. Monastic orders, crusades, and missionary activity spread the Catholic faith across continents, while cathedrals and art expressed the grandeur of divine worship. Despite periods of corruption and reform, Catholicism remained the unifying spiritual force of medieval Europe, influencing law, education, and moral life. It continues to represent a universal community of believers guided by the Pope and the traditions of the early Church. -->
  <BA_Poland_NobleHouse.ideoDescription>天主教是基督教最大的分支，其起源可追溯至耶稣基督的教义以及被视为首位教皇的圣彼得的使徒传承。该教派以罗马为中心，受教廷管辖，在整个中世纪发展成为西方基督教的主导形式，塑造了欧洲的精神、文化与政治根基。天主教会强调圣经与传统的权威，并由教会训导权予以维护。信仰与理性被视为通往神圣真理的互补路径，这一观点深深植根于托马斯·阿奎那、希波的奥古斯丁等中世纪神学家的经院哲学思想中。中世纪天主教的显著特征包括繁复的仪式、对圣徒的崇敬，以及强调通过信仰、善功和参与圣礼获得救赎。修道院团体、十字军东征与传教活动将天主教信仰传播至各大洲，而大教堂与艺术作品则彰显了神圣崇拜的庄严宏伟。尽管经历了腐败与改革的起伏时期，天主教仍是中世纪欧洲统一的精神力量，对法律、教育与道德生活产生了深远影响。如今，它仍是一个由教皇及早期教会传统引领的全球性信徒共同体。</BA_Poland_NobleHouse.ideoDescription>
